# Secrets
.env

# Rust build artifacts. target-cov/ is the worktree-local CARGO_TARGET_DIR
# used to isolate coverage runs when agents build in parallel; target-local/
# is the same idea for whole parallel agent builds; target-push/ likewise for
# the pre-push gate (hooks/pre-push), keeping its fmt/clippy/test off the
# shared cache so it always builds the tree being pushed — without these
# entries a `git add -A` sweeps their build files into the commit.
/target
/target-cov
/target-local
/target-push

# Per-worktree build-cache pointer, generated by hooks/post-checkout
/.cargo/

# Claude Code local settings
.claude/settings.local.json
